>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `CS_STEP_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.CS_STEP_TAC : clasetLib.claset -> NTactical.ntactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Constructs the claset-explicit form of `STEP_TAC`.

`CS_STEP_TAC cs` safely saturates the state. If no safe step applies, it tries
the instantiating cascade on the first goal and considers unsafe rules only
when that cascade is empty. Safe and unsafe wrappers participate. Results
are replayed and may contain residual goals.

Unlike `STEP_TAC`, this interface uses a prepared rule set, exposes the
ntactic result sequence, and does not process theorem-list markers.

### Failure

Produces no result if no safe, instantiating or unsafe transition applies.
Replay failure is reported as an error.

### Example

``` hol4
val step = classicalLib.CS_STEP_TAC (clasetLib.the_claset ());
```

